cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite both the paper and the software.
title: >-
  Replication package for "The Price of Risk When Aggregation Fails:
  Relative Wealth Concerns with Heterogeneous Risk Aversion"
abstract: >-
  Self-contained numerical verification of the results in the paper: the
  neutrality theorem under common risk aversion, the mean-field aggregation
  limit, the frequency of sign reversal in random influence networks, and the
  block replication showing that reversal survives at arbitrary population size.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vicente
    given-names: Renato
    email: rvicente@ime.usp.br
    affiliation: >-
      Instituto de Matemática, Estatística e Ciência da Computação,
      Universidade de São Paulo
license: MIT
keywords:
  - relative wealth concerns
  - keeping up with the Joneses
  - CARA aggregation
  - Katz-Bonacich centrality
  - homophily
